Howdy,

A couple years ago I got ahold of a very PDP-ish minicomputer.  It is 
called a Ford-Higgins PowerFrame.  It was made around '85.  It has the
Q-Bus and uses DEC and other compatible hardware.  The only manuals I have 
for this machine are for the previous model which had a PDP 11/23+ processor.
Mine, however, has a Motorola 68010 processor.  The CPU appears to have been
made by DEC.  Although it has no "M-number", the handles say "Manufactured
by Digital Equipment Corporation"  It appears to me that they were made by
DEC for sale to a second party.  I need to find documentation on this 
board before I can nurse my machine back to health.  Having some spare
parts available, I have by some form of voodoo managed to keep it alive 
this long, and learned a little about hardware in the process.  But, as 
Fred Sanford would say, this may be the "big one" :-).

There is what appears to be a ROM based startup system for entering boot
commands.  Once you turn on the CPU, you are given a "." prompt.  I know
how to tell the machine to boot from the fixed disk (which is also the
effect of toggling the boot switch), but cannot boot from the removeable 
cartridge disk.  I need to find out the commands available to this thing.  
I would also like to find out what the jumper settings are.

