How do I get permission to copy an antique DEC manual.

These days, photocopying places are quite strict about copyright notices,
and even though it's been years since DEC sold an RX01 disk drive, the
copyright notice on the maintenance manual is dated 1976 and it won't
expire for some years to come.

This actually might translate to a call for a new category of copyright
applying to such things as owner's manuals for cars, computers, and other
products with only a limited market lifetime.  Patents protect for only
seven years, but copyrights are for the author's lifetime.  What we need
is something like a technical copyright that expires the way a patent
expires instead of lasting practically forever.

