Well, yes and no :-)

[It's sort of funny following up on a theme that I started. As you might
guess, we have already done this sort of thing with a Wren drive. This
question gets asked often enough, perhaps it should be in the FAQ].

Back to the details. In installing Ultrix onto a third-party disk
[please note that this is an unsupported configuration. I can understand
DEC not supporting this given the wide variety of SCSI devices, but I
wish that there was a way of installing without doing the following
hacks....] you need to start the installation in the normal manner and
select an advanced installation. Follow the bouncing ball, answering the
prompts as appropriate. You will be prompted to choose the disk to
install Ultrix on. Choose your third party disk and wait for the error
(related to the disk being unsupported). Exit the installation procedure
and edit install.1, replacing (in my case) RZ57 with RZxx (the Wren
identifies itself as an RZxx). Restart the install, and all should go
well.

All this is from an increasingly flakey memory (I got parity at birth
where ECC would have been better :-).

Hope this helps.

