The 3200/3500 used the KA650, not the KA630; see my (slightly) earlier
posting.  The note about different PROM versions is apropos for the KA650,
although the only difference was in how the system identified itself;
there was no hardware constraint on the number of logins.  That was
handled by the operating system once it knew which type of CPU board it
was running on.

The KA640 was used in the 3300/3400, and included integrated Ethernet and
DSSI, plus 4MB (?) of onboard memory.

