Perhaps Ultrix uses the "new" 4.3BSD talk.  Sun (at least thru SunOS 4.1.1)
furnished the old 4.2BSD version of talk.  They two are incompatible.
If /etc/services contains only
talk	517/udp     that is the old talk
If /etc/services contains also
ntalk	518/udp	    that is the new talk

Ultrix machines have an otalk command for using the old talk protocol, but
it is sensitive to byte order so rarely works between different kinds of
machines.

We compiled the 4.3BSD talk on Suns and made that the talk command.
