Nothing particular that I know of.  From what little I've seen of them
look like good VAX workstation.  I think they're around as fast as the
DECstation 3100 and slower DECstation 5000s and probably use less memory
per program.
  
>Is DEC phasing out VAX/Ultrix?

No, but a lot of our customers did.  So many that for some systems
there was little reason do the extra work to support new systems, when
the time could be put into supporting new MIPS systems.  I think
the VAX 9000 and VAX 6000-500 got included in V4.2 because there
were enough customer that wanted VAX server systems and vectors on
the VAX 9000 to make the work reasonably profitable.

