> catalogue, indicate that these are probably a master and slave tape unit,
> 1600 bpi.  I have no idea what the physical layout is (but I'm guessing
> huge) or what controller interface they want to see.  I'd like to use it on
> a VME-bus unix machine (none-DEC).  Any information on whether or not this
> is at all feasible would be greatly appreciated.  If they can use a VME
> controller, I'd have to look for a used one of those also.

  The TU77 is an 800/1600 unit. The TU78 is 1600/6250. They both have a
Massbus interface (on the master units). The TU79 is the same drive as
the TU78 with some updates applied and a new door because a customer that
bought many more than DEC (the drive is made by TA/Pertec) wanted a more
IBM-styled door. The TA78 and TA79 are STI (HSC) interface versions of the
TU78 and TU79.

  These are floor-standing units and not light. The bare drive is a Pertec
interface unit (unformatted), although you might need to buy a new inter-
connect card to get "standard Pertec", though all of the signals you need
are in there. You'd then need to get a 1600/6250 formatter card and the
appropriate bus interface.

  You could probably pick up a used Cipher drive (either 1600/3200 or 1600/
6250) with a formatter for less than the cost of a Pertec formatter, and it's
a much smaller unit.

