The VAX 9000 still includes microcode implementation of MOST of the h_floating
instructions, including all the computational ones (add, sub, mul, div);  a
few were removed to deal with unexpected code expansion in other areas.  Among
the instructions removed was MOVH, which is the 'test' VMS applies to see if
it should load the h_floating emulator.  Thus, the VAX 9000 uses a mixture
of microcode implementation and macrocode emulation, with the former most
common.

