    I haven't found anything else in this thread, so please pardon me if this
    has already been mentioned..

    There is a way to clear the SPD (Spin-up Disable) bit for at least some of
    the Digital RZ series drives.  I was able to get it work on a RZ55, but
    not on an RZ57 - your mileage may vary.

    The procedure I have requires a VAXstation 3100 system and the infamous
    Red Spoon (MMJ loopback).  One inserts the Red Spoon, cycles power, and

     >>> t 73

    Answer the questions about port and ID of the drive; then

     RUsure? 42000001

    The test may or may not fail, but it *should* clear the SPD bit.

    The rune to set the SPD bit is

     RUsure? 41000001

    When you're all done, remove the Red Spoon and cycle power again, to clear
    the Deep Magic (field-service) mode.

