In article <SPA.92Jul6170004@khore-dump.fct.unl.pt>, spa@fct.unl.pt (Salvador Pinto Abreu) writes:
> Anyone know if this is possible? If so, what needs to be done? I'm
> willing to get a new controller for the PC (the disks were *real*
> cheap :-).

  Yes. The drives will work with many controllers "as is". The drive has 8
heads and 1024 cylinders. Note that the default for DEC is drive select 3
(of 4) enabled and for most PC's it's 2 (of 4). There is a jumper on the
drive that sets this (and it's labeled, even).

  For some controllers, you may have to remove a 0 ohm jumper (brown body,
single black band) located at position R7 on the drive logic board.

  The 1325 may work with an RLL controller, the 1335 will not. Neither is
certified for RLL operation, by the way.

