The VS2000 was one of the worst boxes I ever had to work in.  I nearly always
got stuck with the duty of installing RD series drives because I have small
hands (an asset when working inside one of these beasts).  Once we opened up
a brand new one, just in from DEC, and I found a paper clip attached to the
insulating sheet that keeps the motherboard from coming in contact with the
case.  It was touching several traces.  If we'd powered it up...

