Just an update on my experiences with this drive.  I was able to eventually
get it to spin-up on power-on and work with my Amiga.  I never discovered if
it was possible to reconfigure the drive via jumpers but someone sent me
an Amiga program which let me permanently reconfigure the drive.  I alos
learned that the drive could have been reconfigured using a program called
'rzdisk' on a DecStation supposedely.  It would be great if in the future
C= could modify their controller to send spin-up commands to drives that
need them.  If anyone's interested this drive maxes out at about 1.4 megs/sec
transfer rate on my 3000.

