If you are running VMS V5.5, you can install VMS POSIX which includes a true
implementation of vi.  The following command will allow vi access from DCL:

	$ vi = "POSIX/RUN POSIX$BIN:VI."
	$ vi yourfile

This is a supported by Digital way of using the vi editor, however it is not
public domain, but I suspect that wasn't your real concern.

