In article <1992Jul9.210017.11172@sei.cmu.edu>, carters@ajpo.sei.cmu.edu (Scott Carter) writes:
> 
> a) which VAXen handle H in emulation; and

I can speak for the following processors using emulation:

- MicroVAX II chipset, used in MicroVAX II and 2000.
- CVAX chipset used in VAXstation 3100 and some other 3000-series
- SOC cpu used in newer VAXstation 3100, VXT2000, etc.
- Mariah cpu used in VAXstation 4000/60, VAX 65xx, 3100/80, etc.

As far as I can determine, as soon as the Age Of The MicroVAX arrived, 
H-floating in hardware was dropped right along with packed decimal.

BTW, Alpha also does not do H-floating in hardware. Doesn't do packed
decimal, either.

