One node in my VAXcluster is on the other side of a bridge (a good ol'
LAN Bridge 100) and has NEVER experienced any timeouts or sluggishness
whatsover.

Note that a bridge introduces a delay of around .5-1ms per frame,
while a repeater is more on the order of - what? 30ns?  So it seems
obvious to me that the "latency" introduced by your repeaters is 
irrelevant.  You probably just have a plain old misconfigured Ethernet
... too many repeaters, too much dB loss on a UTP run, SQE mis-set
somewhere, or what have you.

However, I *would* like to know exactly what LAVC expects for network
performance.  When does it timeout a packet?  How often does it retransmit?
When does it decide to CLUEXIT a node?  My guess would be something like:
timeout after 1 sec, retransmit every 1 sec, CLUEXIT after can't see your
buddies after RECNXINTERVAL.  Does anyone know for sure?

