Doug,

  This is not one of my favorite enclosures. I haven't had to disassemble or
assemble one of these in several years, but:

	* Remove the four screws.

	* The front cover does not need to be removed prior to sliding the
	  entire cover off.

	* The cover has an EXTREMELY tight fit and I frequently had to pry
	  them apart from the back plastic.

	* When you go to re-assemble the cover, the top will probably bow
	  inward and you will have to lift it up to let it slide onto the
	  back assembly (you will invariably catch the tips of your fingers
	  while doing this..I always did).

  Now you know why I was sooo happy when the DS5000/200 was designed to be
opened with a single thumb screw (which immediately prompted the univeristy
folks to ask us for lock mounts in the next box designs).


