I *strongly* recommend you investigate Epoch Systems servers.  The
new Epoch-2 systems are Sparc-II based, and support the HP Optical Library
Units.  But the real value added from Epoch is the layered software--
volume management, migration, backup, database.  We have an Epoch-1
(older hardware, equivalent software) -- for 3 years now -- and an Epoch-2
and are very happy with them.  They seem to be very active in the 
IEEE Mass Storage Committee, and are *very* responsive to customers (I
call them all the time :-)  [betas, ya know]).  

The DEC "StorageServer" is, according to what I have read, based on 
a product from Zetaco, about which I know nothing.  I would note, however,
that Epoch *is* the market leader, and have many installations at large
data consumers (oil companies, e.g., make/eat *lots* of data, and all the
majors seem to have at least one Epoch; the telephone companies, national
labs, RAND, Xerox, GTE, .... all have 'em).

